# D50 (Khoa, 2026-09-23): the standing forge loop's run parameters. tools/deploy.py ships this file to
# /opt/wq/forge.env (PLAN), plans the post-push smoke with exactly these values, and a rollback restores the
# previous copy with the code, so turning the pass-first branch on or off is a deploy (round 3 S5).
# Values copied from the wq-forge unit, read-only `systemctl show wq-forge -p Environment`, 2026-09-23 21:30 +07:
#   N=300 ROUNDS=100000 "FORGE_ARGS=--mode composites --order USA/d1,d1 --no-split --delays 1 --ab new"
# (ROUNDS stays in the unit: it says how long the loop lives, not how a round runs.)
#
# FORMAT, one form only, because two parsers read it: bash (vps/forge_loop.sh sources it) and, once the one-time
# attended install in vps/systemd_wq-forge.service is done, systemd (EnvironmentFile=). Each line is a comment or
# KEY=VALUE with the value bare (no spaces, no shell characters) or in double quotes holding no " \ $ or `.
# systemd.exec(5), systemd 259 on the host: a double-quoted value takes POSIX double-quote escapes, so such a
# value reads the same in both. tools/deploy.py refuses any other line, any other key, a control character anywhere
# in the file, a spending flag, --seed (forge_loop.sh gives each round its own) and --plan (a one-round caller's,
# never the standing loop's: draw5_build release MINOR 8).
#
# THE D54 PROOF WINDOW (Khoa, D47/D53/D54/D60). Once forge/runner.py has `--mode randomised` -- each round's arm drawn
# from sha256(f"{et_day}:{seed}"), even -> composites, odd -> gen, stamped meta.arm_by = "randomiser" -- the window is
# STARTED by replacing `--mode composites` with `--mode randomised` on the FORGE_ARGS line below and pushing
# (tools/deploy.py push: published, venv-checked, smoked with exactly this line, rolled back with the code, D50). It
# is ENDED the same way, back to `--mode composites`. Nothing else starts it: rounds planned with an explicit
# --mode composites|gen stamp arm_by "explicit" and never enter D54's comparison (D60). The runner's owner states
# which of the other flags on the line apply under --mode randomised; change the mode word alone unless they do.
# NOT STARTED: the live value below is still the incumbent's (2026-09-24).
# What the push can and cannot show for that flip (EX-ANTE, from the interface above): the smoke's planner runs ONE
# seed, so it plans whichever arm that seed draws, and `deploy.py watch` ends at the first round that did work, of
# either arm. A crash confined to the other arm's planner passes the smoke, and the watch rolls it back only when a
# round of that arm comes before the first round that did work.
N=300
FORGE_ARGS="--mode composites --order USA/d1,d1 --no-split --delays 1 --ab new"
